description:
Motivation: downstream applications need to programmatically choose models not just by name/size but by explicit capability flags for streaming stability, function-calling profiles, structured-output schema enforcement, and region-aware pricing tiers. This PR extends the model catalog API and the OpenAI-compat shim so clients can filter and route to models with guarantees (or tradeoffs) documented in the capability fields. Summary of changes: 1) Add capability flags to /models and /models/{id} responses: streaming_stability, function_call_profiles, structured_output_schemas, openai_compat_level, and pricing_tiers_by_region. 2) Introduce filter/query params: supports_streaming_stability, supports_function_profile, supports_schema_serialization, openai_compat_min, and region_pricing_tier to the model listing endpoint. 3) Update the OpenAI compatibility layer to advertise shim compatibility levels (none, partial, full) and to expose function-calling profile hints that map to runtime behavior (tiny/standard/extended). 4) Documentation and SDK surface updates (Python + TS) to consume the new fields. 5) Backfill lightweight unit tests and end-to-end smoke test for the listing filters to prevent regressions in search index. Backwards compatibility: All new fields are additive and optional. Clients that do not opt into the new filters will see no behavior change. The OpenAI-compat level is returned as a human-readable string and numeric score for ease of client-side logic. Migration notes: - Catalog indexers will start populating pricing_tiers_by_region from config in the next deploy; a small subset of models will return an empty tiers map until indexer rollout completes. - Feature flag rollout: gating via ff/model-capability-fields; default off for private deployments until ops toggles. API examples: - GET /v1/models?supports_streaming_stability=true&region_pricing_tier=standard returns models marked streaming_stability: "high" or "medium" and pricing_tiers_by_region.[region] == "standard" - Model response snippet (abbreviated): {
  "id": "redwood/s-moderate-8x",
  "capabilities": {
    "streaming_stability": "high",
    "function_call_profiles": ["standard","extended"],
    "structured_output_schemas": ["json_schema_v1"],
    "openai_compat_level": "partial",
    "pricing_tiers_by_region": {"us-west-2":"standard","eu-central-1":"premium"}
  }
}
Testing: unit tests for serializer/deserializer, integration tests for listing filters, and a small perf guard to ensure catalog query latency stays within 2x baseline. Rollout plan: feature flag + canary on model-indexer then 2-step deploy for API servers (read-only first, read-write after indexers).
